I am finally in Berlin.
I pull my suitcase outside through the sliding door.
The suitcase is very heavy.
It is January.
The evening is dark and extremely cold.
I am freezing immediately.
I need a taxi.
But where is the taxi rank?
I see a man in an airport uniform.
"Excuse me," I say to him.
"Are you an employee here?"
"Yes, I am," the man answers.
"Where are there taxis here?" I ask.
"The taxi rank is over there," he says.
He looks at me.
"Are you freezing?" he asks kindly.
"Yes, very much," I answer.
"I come from Mexico," I explain.
"It is warm there."
The man laughs.
"Welcome to winter!" he says.
"Thank you," I say and walk to the taxis.
